    rdf:value """The first 6-7 lines of p. 111 and p. 112 cut away
[Thursday April 29. 1897.]
We saw the museo of Forlì, and made acquaintance with the painter, Baldassare Carrari. 
Bernhard says my idea of freedom is “ the lack of inhibition to an impulse .”
Friday April 30. 1897. Risorgimento. Bari 
Saw Trani and Giovinazzo, and came here. At Giovinazzo we found a Lotto for sale – the middle panel of a triptych, a seated bishop. Late and in poor condition. Saw Bari. """^^xsd:string ;
